  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Strings",
      "h2": "Bowed Family",
      "body_html": "<p>The orchestra <strong>string</strong> family is <strong>violin, viola, cello, double bass</strong> — biggest to smallest in tone. Strings are bowed, plucked or struck.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Wind",
      "h2": "Woodwind Family",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Woodwind</strong> includes <strong>flute, oboe, clarinet, bassoon</strong>. Many were once made of wood. Sound comes from blowing across or through a reed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Reeds",
      "h2": "Single & Double",
      "body_html": "<p>The <strong>clarinet</strong> has a <strong>single reed</strong>. The <strong>oboe</strong> and <strong>bassoon</strong> have <strong>double reeds</strong>. The <strong>flute</strong> has no reed — you blow across an edge.</p>"
    }
  ],
